    {
      "text": "Preheat an outdoor grill for medium heat and lightly oil the grate.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": []
    },
    {
      "text": "Combine ground pork, ground beef, ground lamb, and egg white in a large bowl.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/dhnHJbN9G0x66I4BU3D3W0vJvQQ=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/80398_SerbianCevapcici_ddmfs_Step2_3x4_3415-32d0bf9d701947c680d20cb0c25c6688.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/80398/step_03.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Add garlic, black pepper, salt, baking soda, cayenne pepper, and paprika. Mix well using your hands; form into finger-length sausages about 3/4-inch thick.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/HyaEFYgfh3DWw6XhmOLf9SZhJiA=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/80398_SerbianCevapcici_ddmfs_Step4_3x4_3431-1b0949e0da8e4907b366017dbe07a133.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/80398/step_04.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Cook sausages on the preheated grill, turning occasionally, until no longer pink in the center, about 30 minutes. An instant-read thermometer inserted into the center should read 160 degrees F (70 degrees C).",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
